# Generated Flutter desktop plugin-registrant files are always written with LF
# line endings by `flutter pub get`, regardless of platform or the developer's
# `core.autocrlf` setting. They are stored here with LF, so on a machine with
# core.autocrlf=true they check out as CRLF and the very next `flutter pub get`
# rewrites them back to LF — every example app then shows as "modified" in
# `git status` even though nothing meaningful changed.
#
# Pinning eol=lf keeps the checked-out bytes identical to what `pub get`
# regenerates, so these paths stay clean regardless of the developer's autocrlf
# setting. Patterns rather than a path list because this repo holds nine Flutter
# apps (five package examples, plus example_chat/example_perf and super_clones/)
# and gains more over time.
#
# Reported as MemNote NOTE-144; the same fix on the MemNote side is NOTE-132.
**/linux/flutter/generated_plugin_registrant.cc text eol=lf
**/linux/flutter/generated_plugin_registrant.h text eol=lf
**/linux/flutter/generated_plugins.cmake text eol=lf
**/windows/flutter/generated_plugin_registrant.cc text eol=lf
**/windows/flutter/generated_plugin_registrant.h text eol=lf
**/windows/flutter/generated_plugins.cmake text eol=lf
**/macos/Flutter/GeneratedPluginRegistrant.swift text eol=lf
